            "result_text": "Done! I've created `/app/run.py` with the `run_tasks` function that:\n\n**Key features:**\n- ✅ Runs async tasks with a configurable concurrency limit using `asyncio.Semaphore`\n- ✅ Handles keyboard interrupts gracefully: cancels tasks and waits for their cleanup code to run (finally blocks, context manager exits)\n- ✅ Propagates exceptions from tasks while ensuring cleanup\n- ✅ Can be imported as `from run import run_tasks`\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Wraps each task with a semaphore to limit concurrency\n2. On `KeyboardInterrupt`, explicitly cancels all task objects\n3. Uses `gather(..., return_exceptions=True)` to wait for them to finish cleanup\n4. Re-raises the interrupt so your code knows it was interrupted\n\n**Verified with tests showing:**\n- Concurrent limit enforced (max 2 concurrent with `max_concurrent=2`)\n- Cleanup runs even on exceptions\n- Cleanup runs even when tasks are cancelled"
